	(text "Layout: TP9-TP12 are bring-up test pads, not fitted (#36).\nTP11 (SW): put it on the U1 PH / L1 copper with no stub; keep the SW area small.\nTP12 (GND): next to C15 / U1 GND, as the scope ground for TP9-TP11." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 81.28 186.69 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid "b5d2ad61-b6ea-478b-aac4-500effa7b944"))
	(text "Layout: keep the buck switching loops small (D59 p23-24, #63).\nD1 SS34 close to U1 PH (pin 8) and the U1 GND area: loop PH - D1 - GND - C15 as small as possible.\nL1 very close to U1 PH; keep the SW copper (PH, D1, L1, C16) small.\nC16 (boot cap) close to U1 BOOT (pin 1) and PH, short traces.\nOutput loop PH - L1 - C17/C35/C36 - GND as small as practical; GND vias at the cap ground ends." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 101.6 63.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "8fbaaeb2-af71-4948-8285-2e548aded57a"))
	(text "Layout: VSNS trace from the R10/R11/R27 divider to U1 VSENSE\n(pin 4): keep it away from the SW node (U1 PH, D1, L1). Route it\nunder the output caps or on another layer (D59 p23-24, #63)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 185.42 88.9 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "2af230af-3de6-4717-bdc4-dbfc2c7f8d22"))
)
